    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nExceptional 0.5acre Coastal Site with Panoramic Sea Views at Croaghcross, Portsalon, Co. Donegal.\n\nAn outstanding opportunity to acquire a beautifully positioned site extending to approximately 0.5acres in one of Donegal's most sought-after coastal locations. \nElevated to maximise its spectacular outlook, the site enjoys uninterrupted panoramic views across Lough Swilly, with the dramatic Inishowen Peninsula forming a stunning backdrop.\n\nThe site offers excellent development potential for either a prestigious one off residence or small multi-unit \ndevelopment, subject to the necessary planning permission.\n\nThis is a rare opportunity to secure a prime coastal site in an area renowned for its outstanding natural beauty, making it ideal for those seeking a peaceful retreat or an investment in one of Donegal's most desirable seaside destinations.\n\nNestled on the edge of the picturesque village of Portsalon, this attractive parcel offers an idyllic setting for a permanent residence or holiday home (subject to the necessary planning permission). \n\nThe site combines privacy and tranquillity with the convenience of nearby amenities, including the renowned Ballymastocker Beach, Portsalon Pier, local shops, cafés, and the celebrated Portsalon Golf Club. \nBallymastocker Beach is widely regarded as one of Ireland's finest beaches and is located along the scenic Wild Atlantic Way."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li>Key Features</li><li> Circa 0.5 acres (Folio DL50769F)</li><li> Elevated site with magnificent panoramic sea views </li><li> Overlooking Lough Swilly and the Inishowen Peninsula </li><li> Walking distance to Portsalon village amenities </li><li> Close to Ballymastocker Beach, Portsalon Pier and Portsalon Golf Club </li><li> Peaceful coastal setting with excellent road frontage </li><li> Superb opportunity for a private residence or holiday home (subject to planning permission) </li><li> Located along the spectacular Wild Atlantic Way </li><li> All services (water/electricity) abut the property.</li><li> Previously had planning permission for 3 no. terrace properties this planning permission has since lapsed.</ul>"
      },
      {
